---
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
	title={`Privacy Policy | ${AUTHOR_NAME}`}
	description="How this site handles data: hosting, comments, and why there is no cookie banner."
>
	<div class="page-head">
		<div class="container page-head__inner">
			<Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="meta">
				This applies regardless of the site's language, since the site is operated from Germany and
				GDPR applies to the operator, not the visitor.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Responsible party</h2>
				<p>
					Sebastian Koch, Industriestraße 29, 82194 Gröbenzell, Germany.{' '}
					<a href="mailto:sebastian.koch@consos.de">sebastian.koch@consos.de</a>. See the{' '}
					<a href="/imprint">imprint</a> for full details.
				</p>

				<h2>Hosting</h2>
				<p>
					This site is hosted on Cloudflare's network. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes
					technical connection data for every request, such as IP address, browser type, and
					timestamp, in order to deliver the site and to protect it against abuse. This happens
					automatically and is not something this site's code controls directly. Cloudflare acts
					as a data processor here and publishes its own{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a
					> and data processing terms, including safeguards for international data transfers.
				</p>

				<h2>Fonts</h2>
				<p>
					This site uses the Newsreader, Work Sans and JetBrains Mono typefaces, downloaded once
					at build time and served from this site's own domain. Your browser never contacts Google
					or any other font provider when you visit this site.
				</p>

				<h2>Theme preference</h2>
				<p>
					If you switch between the light and dark theme, that choice is saved in your browser's
					local storage under the key <code>sc-theme</code>. It stays on your device, is never
					sent to a server, and exists only so the site does not forget your preference between
					visits. Clearing your browser storage removes it.
				</p>

				<h2>Comments</h2>
				<p>
					Articles have an optional comment section. If you post a comment, the name you choose to
					enter, the comment text, and the time of posting are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database
					so the comment can be displayed. I do not store your IP address alongside comments. New
					comments are held in a private moderation queue and only become publicly visible after I
					review them; rejected comments are deleted rather than published.
				</p>
				<p>
					The comment form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a captcha alternative that helps
					block automated spam. The Turnstile script only loads on article pages that show a
					comment form, not sitewide, and only runs when you interact with the form. Your browser
					sends your IP address to Cloudflare as part of that verification; this site does not
					receive or store it. Turnstile is used because it is necessary to provide the commenting
					feature you are actively using, not for tracking.
				</p>

				<h2>No analytics, no advertising</h2>
				<p>
					This site runs no analytics, advertising, or marketing scripts, and sets no tracking
					cookies. Because of that, there is no cookie consent banner: nothing non-essential is
					loaded that would require your consent under the ePrivacy rules. If that ever changes,
					this page and a consent mechanism will be updated accordingly.
				</p>

				<h2>External links</h2>
				<p>
					Where articles link to external sites (for example, Microsoft's documentation), those
					sites have their own privacy policies that this policy does not cover.
				</p>

				<h2>Your rights</h2>
				<p>
					Under GDPR you have the right to access, correct, or delete data concerning you, to
					restrict or object to its processing, and to data portability. If you posted a comment
					and want it edited or removed, email{' '}
					<a href="mailto:sebastian.koch@consos.de">sebastian.koch@consos.de</a> with a link to the
					page and I will take care of it. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
					protection supervisory authority.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		background: var(--bg-band);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
		padding-block: 2.5rem 3rem;
	}

	.page-head__inner {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 62ch;
	}
</style>
